WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:05.580
The hype for Avengers Infinity War is reaching
boiling point and Kevin Feige has now confirmed

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:08.350
there are going to be real character deaths
in the movie.

00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:12.820
Yippee-ki-yay movie lovers, it's Jan and in
this video, I'm going to explain why I think

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:17.279
one specific character that hasn't typically
appeared on everyone's death-lists will be

00:00:17.279 --> 00:00:19.019
killed by Thanos in the film.

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:23.900
I'm also starting a new Marvel giveaway – to
enter, make sure you're a subscriber and tell

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:28.010
me in the comments who you think won't make
it out of Infinity War alive.

00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:31.320
And I'll announce the winner of my last giveaway
later in this video.

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:35.760
Obviously, speculation and potential spoilers
ahead for Infinity War.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:40.140
It's generally thought that Marvel are going
to hit fans big in Avengers Infinity War and

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:42.410
kill off someone like Cap or Iron Man.

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:46.820
After all, Tony did have that vision in Age
of Ultron of his fellow heroes strewn lifeless

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:48.620
on a rock in outer space.

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:53.230
But a recent EW interview with Josh Brolin
who plays Thanos has got me thinking that

00:00:53.230 --> 00:00:56.330
it won't be a main Avenger who we lose in
Infinity War.

00:00:56.330 --> 00:01:00.870
When Brolin was asked about Thanos's daughters,
Nebula and Gamora, the actor found it difficult

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:02.090
to discuss.

00:01:02.090 --> 00:01:07.130
Although he did say the Mad Titan treats both
Gamora and Nebula as tools for his own gain,

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:10.580
when pushed on whether Thanos is "cold the
whole way through, or [if] he feel[s] any

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:12.930
affection for them?", this is what Brolin
said:

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:13.930
"Yeah.

00:01:13.930 --> 00:01:14.999
I do think he does.

00:01:14.999 --> 00:01:19.210
When you see the relationship with Gamora
and you see that evolves, God I wish I could

00:01:19.210 --> 00:01:20.210
tell you.

00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:21.210
I can't!

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:24.939
Obviously he has a grand plan, like somebody
who's pulling in kids for their own selfish

00:01:24.939 --> 00:01:26.079
bloodshed.

00:01:26.079 --> 00:01:29.159
But he has a capacity to love very much and
very deeply."

00:01:29.159 --> 00:01:33.319
Now, I think it's very interesting that Brolin
specifically mentioned Gamora but tried to

00:01:33.319 --> 00:01:37.259
stop himself from revealing anything further
in terms of bigger plot points.

00:01:37.259 --> 00:01:41.950
We need to remember that Gamora is Thanos's
favourite daughter and that favouritism has

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:45.400
been something that has been very painful
for her adoptive sister Nebula.

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:50.429
"Your demeanor is that of a pouty child."

00:01:50.429 --> 00:01:55.450
"And, apparently, you alienated my favorite
daughter, Gamora."

00:01:55.450 --> 00:01:57.649
So, why would Thanos kill Gamora?

00:01:57.649 --> 00:02:02.079
Well, there's rumours that if Thanos does
get to all six Infinity Stones, he'll still

00:02:02.079 --> 00:02:05.490
need something extra to be able to use the
Soul Stone.

00:02:05.490 --> 00:02:09.890
That particular Infinity Stone still hasn't
been revealed in the MCU, though I've talked

00:02:09.890 --> 00:02:14.500
about possible locations where it could appear
in my Soul Stone video, but the idea is that

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:18.480
to be able to use the Soul Stone you have
to sacrifice someone you love.

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:23.319
Thanos has a twisted love for his daughters,
and Gamora is his favourite, which could mean

00:02:23.319 --> 00:02:26.209
Thanos will kill her in order to control the
Soul Stone.

00:02:26.209 --> 00:02:29.730
But before you get too upset, just remember
we're talking comic book movies here, and

00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:34.120
it's quite likely that the Infinity War sequel
will involve the Avengers trying to reverse

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:37.470
some of the events from Infinity War, perhaps
with time travel.

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:42.380
As for Marvel, killing Gamora would indeed
give their film an emotional hit, without

00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:47.319
their having to retire one of the original
core characters like Iron Man or Cap at this

00:02:47.319 --> 00:02:48.319
point.

00:02:48.319 --> 00:02:51.819
And there's actually a bit of supporting evidence
for this idea in the form of one of the Infinity

00:02:51.819 --> 00:02:57.390
War LEGO sets for the final battle in which
Iron Man, Gamora and Star-Lord face off against

00:02:57.390 --> 00:02:59.750
Thanos who is wielding an Infinity Sword.

00:02:59.750 --> 00:03:03.659
We don't know how this battle will go, but
it could be the moment in which Thanos carries

00:03:03.659 --> 00:03:05.540
out his dastardly deed.

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:09.840
After all we do see Iron Man extremely upset
in this shot from the first trailer and it

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:13.340
looks like it could be set on Thanos's home
world Titan.

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:17.810
We also know that in Guardians of the Galaxy
Vol. 2, Nebula came to terms with her sister

00:03:17.810 --> 00:03:22.239
Gamora and seeing Thanos kill her would be
the final straw, setting up a huge revenge

00:03:22.239 --> 00:03:24.200
story for her in Avengers 4.

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:28.459
"There are little girls like you across the
universe who are in danger."

00:03:28.459 --> 00:03:31.330
"You can stay with us and help them."

00:03:31.330 --> 00:03:33.719
"I will help them by killing Thanos."

00:03:33.719 --> 00:03:36.530
"I don't know if that's possible."

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:40.010
"You will always be my sister."

00:03:40.010 --> 00:03:44.069
Now, I really like Gamora, so I'll be pretty
devastated if this does play out.

00:03:44.069 --> 00:03:48.671
However, Zoe Saldana has already revealed
she's been filming on Avengers 4, but she

00:03:48.671 --> 00:03:52.739
could have been filming flashback scenes from
before her death or if that movie really does

00:03:52.739 --> 00:03:57.569
reverse the events from Infinity War then,
of course, we might see Gamora come back to

00:03:57.569 --> 00:03:58.569
life.

00:03:58.569 --> 00:04:01.650
The really interesting thing in all this is
that Gamora's death would actually parallel

00:04:01.650 --> 00:04:03.769
something which happened to her in the comics.

00:04:03.769 --> 00:04:08.299
When Gamora discovered Thanos's master plan
to kill off half the universe, she attempted

00:04:08.299 --> 00:04:09.959
to kill him with a dagger.

00:04:09.959 --> 00:04:13.080
However, Thanos mortally wounded her and left
her for dead.

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:17.769
Adam Warlock found Gamora about to die and
to save her he absorbed her spirit into the

00:04:17.769 --> 00:04:21.829
Soul Gem and took her into a place inside
the gem called Soulworld.

00:04:21.829 --> 00:04:26.389
Gamora stayed in Soulworld until the events
of the Infinity Gauntlet when Adam Warlock

00:04:26.389 --> 00:04:31.289
restored Gamora into the real world via the
body of a recently deceased human.

00:04:31.289 --> 00:04:35.110
She died again though when Thanos erased half
of the universe from existence.

00:04:35.110 --> 00:04:39.900
By the way, James Gunn has said we won't be
getting Adam Warlock in the Infinity War movie,

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:44.509
however, he'll likely appear in Guardians
of the Galaxy Vol. 3, and I talk about how

00:04:44.509 --> 00:04:47.880
that will happen in my Adam Warlock teaser
video.

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:52.840
Nebula also plays a key part in the Infinity
Gauntlet storyline and the final defeat of

00:04:52.840 --> 00:04:53.840
Thanos.

00:04:53.840 --> 00:04:57.930
Initially, in the Infinity Gauntlet comics,
Thanos wreaks havoc on Nebula's body, torturing

00:04:57.930 --> 00:05:03.450
her and turning her into a living corpse who
he uses to try to impress Mistress Death.

00:05:03.450 --> 00:05:07.120
Later in the story though, it's Nebula who
turns the balance of power away from Thanos

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:09.610
by taking the gauntlet from him.

00:05:09.610 --> 00:05:13.310
Nebula then restores the half of the universe
which Thanos had killed, which also brings

00:05:13.310 --> 00:05:14.310
back Gamora.

00:05:14.310 --> 00:05:18.259
Now, I don't think this is exactly what will
happen in the movies, however, in this glimpse

00:05:18.259 --> 00:05:23.340
of Nebula from the Super Bowl TV spot, we
can see that she's absolutely furious at something.

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:27.770
Could it be she's just witnessed Thanos appear
to kill her sister Gamora?

00:05:27.770 --> 00:05:32.550
If Nebula, or another character, does reverse
Gamora's death or any other effects of Thanos's

00:05:32.550 --> 00:05:37.690
devastation, that would happen in Avengers
4, not Infinity War, of course.

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:41.770
By the way, another possibility is that Marvel
might do a twist on this idea in the Infinity

00:05:41.770 --> 00:05:47.100
War movie, with Thanos killing Nebula as she
goes up against him, rather than Gamora.

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:51.030
Nebula is still one of his daughters and so
could be used by Thanos to harness the power

00:05:51.030 --> 00:05:55.330
of the Soul Stone, with Gamora then having
to exact revenge on the Mad Titan.

00:05:55.330 --> 00:06:00.320
Either way, if Gamora or Nebula does die,
perhaps by having their souls taken from them

00:06:00.320 --> 00:06:04.440
by Thanos, then this would be quite an emotional
set-up for Avengers 4.

00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:09.530
So, do you think Gamora or Nebula will be
a casualty in Avengers: Infinity War or do

00:06:09.530 --> 00:06:12.340
you have any theories on who else Thanos might
kill?

